From the equation for $x$, $t^2=6-x$.
Substitute into the equation for $y$:
$\begin{align*}y&=(6-x)-2\\y&=4-x.\end{align*}$
The parameter interval gives $0\le t^2\le9$, so the domain is $-3\le x\le6$ and the range is $-2\le y\le7$.
The curve is the line segment joining $(-3,7)$ and $(6,-2)$, with both endpoints included.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,>=stealth]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,draw=black] (-4,0)--(7,0);
\draw[->,draw=black] (0,-3)--(0,8);
\path (7,0) node[right,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\path (0,8) node[above,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$y$};
\draw[draw=curveBlue,line width=0.8pt] (-3,7)--(6,-2);
\fill[fill=curveBlue] (-3,7) circle[radius=1.2pt];
\fill[fill=curveBlue] (6,-2) circle[radius=1.2pt];
\path (-3,7) node[above right,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$(-3,7)$};
\path (6,-2) node[below left,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$(6,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
